  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Clinique Vétérinaire Saint-Antoine is set up at Espace Perdigon, on route de Pégomas in Grasse. It is part of the Mon Véto network, whose official page for the clinic describes a technical platform allowing comprehensive care, with consultations, surgery, an analysis lab, radiology and ultrasound. It treats dogs, cats and small pets. The page shows a rating of 4.7 out of 5 from about 380 reviews.</p>
      <p>The team presented on the page includes six vets and eight specialised assistants. The clinic's page offers online appointment booking.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The clinic is open Monday to Friday from 8am to 7:30pm and Saturday from 8am to 6pm; it is closed on Sunday. On emergencies, the clinic's official page offers a "Contact emergencies" button and a pre-admission form, but does not present a night service. Directories contradict each other: one shows emergencies handled at the clinic 24/7, another says emergencies are transferred to another clinic. Outside opening hours, call the clinic before heading over with your dog.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: keep the clinic's number handy during your stay in Grasse, and always call before heading over outside the listed opening hours.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The clinic is at Espace Perdigon, route de Pégomas, away from the historic centre of Grasse. The clinic's page also offers an online shop.</p>
